[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/comments/1230945602","html_url":"https://github.com/trpc/trpc/issues/2595#issuecomment-1230945602","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/2595","id":1230945602,"node_id":"IC_kwDOELj1_s5JXr1C","user":{"login":"sachinraja","id":58836760,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4ODM2NzYw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/58836760?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sachinraja","html_url":"https://github.com/sachinraja","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sachinraja/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sachinraja/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sachinraja/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sachinraja/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sachinraja/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sachinraja/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sachinraja/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sachinraja/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sachinraja/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-08-29T22:42:13Z","updated_at":"2022-08-30T02:03:09Z","body":"The first function call takes in the generics, the second one takes in the options. This is because TS won't let us partially infer the generics. If we change it to only one function call, users would have to pass in the types for `errorFormatter` and `transformer` if they wanted to pass in any `Context` type.\r\n\r\n> change docs only (change trpcInner to a meaningful function name)\r\n\r\nI think it's easier to just accept the double function call. `trpcInner` would just be a useless variable and increase boilerplate.\r\n\r\n> would it be nice to create a file convention like trpc.config.ts or trpc.router.ts ?\r\n\r\nThe examples follow conventions already.\r\n\r\n> You could also take it one step further and create it as express app.\r\n\r\n`@trpc/server` core is agnostic from Node, this is what adapters are for.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/comments/1230945602/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/comments/1231078330","html_url":"https://github.com/trpc/trpc/issues/2595#issuecomment-1231078330","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/2595","id":1231078330,"node_id":"IC_kwDOELj1_s5JYMO6","user":{"login":"mmkal","id":15040698,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDQwNjk4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15040698?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmkal","html_url":"https://github.com/mmkal","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmkal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmkal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmkal/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmkal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmkal/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmkal/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmkal/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmkal/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmkal/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-08-30T02:47:52Z","updated_at":"2022-08-30T02:47:52Z","body":"Reopening this because I think there's further discussion to be had, and I don't want it to get lost on a closed thread (not implying it was closed improperly, I just have something I want to add).\r\n\r\n@sachinraja @KATT what about naming two functions in some kind of logical way so there isn't this big gulf between users and implementers. Anyone new looking at `initTRPC()()` is going to get intimidated and probably put off. What about something like:\r\n\r\n```ts\r\n// initTRPC.ts\r\nexport interface TRPCBuilder<TParams extends Partial<InitGenerics>> {\r\n    configure: <TNewParams extends TParams>() => TRPCBuilder<TNewParams>\r\n    builder: <\r\n        TOptions extends Partial<InitOptions<{\r\n            ctx: TParams['ctx'] extends undefined ? {} : NonNullable<TParams['ctx']>;\r\n            meta: TParams['meta'] extends undefined ? {} : NonNullable<TParams['meta']>;\r\n        }>>\r\n    >(options?: ValidateShape<TOptions, Partial<InitOptions<{\r\n        ctx: TParams['ctx'] extends undefined ? {} : NonNullable<TParams['ctx']>;\r\n        meta: TParams['meta'] extends undefined ? {} : NonNullable<TParams['meta']>;\r\n    }>>> | undefined) =>  /* same as existing final return type of initTRPC */\r\n}\r\n\r\nexport const trpc: TRPCBuilder<{}>\r\n```\r\n\r\nUsage:\r\n\r\n```ts\r\nimport {trpc} from '@trpc/server'\r\n\r\nconst t = trpc.builder()\r\n\r\nexport const whatever = t.procedure\r\n  .input(z.object({ foo: z.string() })\r\n  .query(({ input }) => [input.foo])\r\n```\r\n\r\nOr with ctx/meta options:\r\n\r\n```ts\r\nimport {trpc} from '@trpc/server'\r\n\r\nconst t = trpc.configure<{ ctx: { abc: number } }>().builder()\r\n\r\nexport const whatever = t.procedure\r\n  .input(z.object({ foo: z.string() })\r\n  .query(({ input, ctx }) => [input.foo, ctx.abc])\r\n```\r\n\r\nNot sure about the naming of either `.configure()` or `.builder()`.\r\n\r\nAnother option would be just to have two methods `.withContext<{ abc: number }>()` and `.withMeta<{ xyz: string }>()` which would add `ctx` and `meta` generics, respectively.\r\n\r\n`.builder()` might not be the best name if `t` shouldn't be considered a builder. (If it isn't - what is it? I think it's important that it has some kind of English-language name, so people can communicate about it properly, since it's an important part of the design - in general I think we should show things we love them by naming them).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/comments/1231078330/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":3,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/comments/1232154649","html_url":"https://github.com/trpc/trpc/issues/2595#issuecomment-1232154649","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/2595","id":1232154649,"node_id":"IC_kwDOELj1_s5JcTAZ","user":{"login":"KATT","id":459267,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1OTI2Nw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/459267?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KATT","html_url":"https://github.com/KATT","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KATT/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KATT/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KATT/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KATT/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KATT/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KATT/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KATT/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KATT/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KATT/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-08-30T20:51:21Z","updated_at":"2022-08-30T20:51:29Z","body":"On one hand, I'm like _\"meh, you do it once, who cares?\"_, and on the other hand I think it's the first interaction you might have with tRPC and it is a bit counter-intuitive\r\n\r\nHow about the words `configure` & `create()` at the end?\r\n\r\n```ts\r\nimport {trpc} from '@trpc/server'\r\n\r\nconst t = trpc.create();\r\nconst t = trpc.configure<{ ctx: {} } >().create()\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\nAlternative, call it `generics()` or something?\r\n\r\n\r\n```ts\r\nimport {trpc} from '@trpc/server'\r\n\r\nconst t = trpc.create();\r\nconst t = trpc.generics<{ ctx: {} } >().create()\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nWe could even do it like it is now but with an extra helper, but it wrecks discoverability a bit:\r\n\r\n```ts\r\nimport {initTRPC} from '@trpc/server'\r\n\r\nconst t = initTRPC();\r\nconst t = initTRPC.withGenerics<{ ctx: {} } >()()\r\n\r\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/comments/1232154649/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/comments/1232158269","html_url":"https://github.com/trpc/trpc/issues/2595#issuecomment-1232158269","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/2595","id":1232158269,"node_id":"IC_kwDOELj1_s5JcT49","user":{"login":"KATT","id":459267,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1OTI2Nw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/459267?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KATT","html_url":"https://github.com/KATT","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KATT/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KATT/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KATT/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KATT/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KATT/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KATT/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KATT/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KATT/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KATT/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-08-30T20:55:21Z","updated_at":"2022-08-30T20:56:51Z","body":"I quite like the idea to make it a proper builder\r\n\r\n```ts\r\nconst t = initTRPC\r\n  .withMeta<{}>()\r\n  .withContext<Context>()\r\n  .create()\r\n```\r\n\r\nor\r\n\r\n```ts\r\nconst t = initTRPC\r\n  .meta<{}>() \r\n  .context<Context>()   // maybe `.ctx<Context>()`?\r\n  .create()\r\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/comments/1232158269/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/comments/1232191079","html_url":"https://github.com/trpc/trpc/issues/2595#issuecomment-1232191079","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/2595","id":1232191079,"node_id":"IC_kwDOELj1_s5Jcb5n","user":{"login":"josvanos","id":58590579,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NTkwNTc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/58590579?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/josvanos","html_url":"https://github.com/josvanos","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/josvanos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/josvanos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/josvanos/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/josvanos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/josvanos/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/josvanos/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/josvanos/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/josvanos/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/josvanos/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-08-30T21:32:01Z","updated_at":"2022-08-30T21:32:01Z","body":"One quick note I wanted to add to this discussion, I have the feeling this proposed builder pattern is way more resistant to future changes than current implementation `initTRPC()()`.  I forgot to address future changes in my first message.\r\n\r\nAbout the builder pattern:  initTRPC is more a function name than an object name, rather just trpc or something like that.\r\nI do not have a preference if it is `.setContext` or `.withContext` or `.useContext` or `.context` , as long as it is consistent.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/comments/1232191079/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/comments/1232224779","html_url":"https://github.com/trpc/trpc/issues/2595#issuecomment-1232224779","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/2595","id":1232224779,"node_id":"IC_kwDOELj1_s5JckIL","user":{"login":"graddotdev","id":4836709,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4MzY3MDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4836709?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/graddotdev","html_url":"https://github.com/graddotdev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graddotdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graddotdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graddotdev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graddotdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graddotdev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graddotdev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graddotdev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graddotdev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graddotdev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-08-30T22:16:30Z","updated_at":"2022-08-30T22:17:03Z","body":"The new `satisfies` operator should help I think: https://github.com/microsoft/TypeScript/issues/47920","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/comments/1232224779/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/comments/1232233790","html_url":"https://github.com/trpc/trpc/issues/2595#issuecomment-1232233790","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/2595","id":1232233790,"node_id":"IC_kwDOELj1_s5JcmU-","user":{"login":"sachinraja","id":58836760,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4ODM2NzYw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/58836760?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sachinraja","html_url":"https://github.com/sachinraja","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sachinraja/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sachinraja/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sachinraja/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sachinraja/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sachinraja/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sachinraja/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sachinraja/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sachinraja/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sachinraja/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-08-30T22:27:58Z","updated_at":"2022-08-30T22:29:08Z","body":"@mmkal Alex and I talked about this, and we're in favor of the builder pattern style (copying from above):\r\n```ts\r\nconst t = initTRPC\r\n  .meta<{}>() \r\n  .context<Context>()   // maybe `.ctx<Context>()`?\r\n  .create()\r\n```\r\n\r\nI think this is better because it removes the object generic in `initTRPC`, which is more confusing than the double call to me.\r\n\r\nNo expectations, but would you be willing to do a PR for this?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/comments/1232233790/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/comments/1232241753","html_url":"https://github.com/trpc/trpc/issues/2595#issuecomment-1232241753","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/2595","id":1232241753,"node_id":"IC_kwDOELj1_s5JcoRZ","user":{"login":"mmkal","id":15040698,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDQwNjk4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15040698?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmkal","html_url":"https://github.com/mmkal","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmkal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmkal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmkal/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmkal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmkal/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmkal/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmkal/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmkal/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmkal/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-08-30T22:38:09Z","updated_at":"2022-08-30T22:38:09Z","body":"Nice - yes I can open a pr. Have been looking for a chance to make a v10 change about this size. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/comments/1232241753/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":3,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{